/-!
# The structure of the rings `D(n)`

Work in an affine crystalline situation `(A, I, γ, C)`, choose a polynomial algebra
`P = A[x_i]` over `A` together with a surjection `P → C` with kernel `J`, and let `D` be the
`p`-adically completed divided power envelope of `J`. For `n ≥ 0` let `J(n)` be the kernel of
the induced surjection `P ⊗_A … ⊗_A P → C` on the `(n + 1)`-fold tensor power and let `D(n)`
be the `p`-adically completed divided power envelope of `J(n)`.

The coprojection `P → P ⊗_A … ⊗_A P`, `h ↦ h ⊗ 1 ⊗ … ⊗ 1`, then induces an isomorphism

  `D(n) = lim_e D⟨ξ_i(j)⟩ / p^e D⟨ξ_i(j)⟩`

of algebras over `D`, where `D⟨ξ_i(j)⟩` is the divided power polynomial algebra over `D` on
the variables

  `ξ_i(j) = x_i ⊗ 1 ⊗ … ⊗ 1 - 1 ⊗ … ⊗ 1 ⊗ x_i ⊗ 1 ⊗ … ⊗ 1`

for `j = 1, …, n`, the second `x_i` sitting in the `(j + 1)`-st slot. The reason is that
`P ⊗_A … ⊗_A P` is the polynomial algebra `P[ξ_i(j)]` over its first tensor factor and `J(n)`
is generated by `J` and the elements `ξ_i(j)`, so the divided power envelope of `J(n)` is the
divided power polynomial algebra on the `ξ_i(j)` over the divided power envelope of `J`.

## Main definitions

* `Crystalline.coprojectionDifference` — the element `ξ_i(j)` of `P ⊗_A … ⊗_A P`.
* `Crystalline.dividedPowerPolynomialOverEnvelope` — the divided power polynomial algebra
  `D⟨ξ_i(j)⟩` over `D`.
* `Crystalline.pAdicCompletedDividedPowerPolynomialOverEnvelope` — its `p`-adic completion
  `lim_e D⟨ξ_i(j)⟩ / p^e D⟨ξ_i(j)⟩`, with structure map
  `Crystalline.toPAdicCompletedDividedPowerPolynomial` from `D` and divided power variables
  `Crystalline.coprojectionDifferenceVariable`.

## Main results

* `Crystalline.exists_ringEquiv_pAdicCompletedDividedPowerPolynomial` — the displayed
  isomorphism of algebras over `D` induced by the coprojection.

## Implementation notes

As in the formalization of the lemma on adjoining variables to a divided power envelope from
which this one is deduced, the displayed equality is expressed as an isomorphism together with
the equations that pin it down. The algebra structure of `D(n)` over `D` is a ring map `φ`
agreeing with the coprojection on the image of `P`, and the isomorphism is required to be an
isomorphism over `φ` carrying the image of `ξ_i(j)` in `D(n)` to the divided power variable
`ξ_i(j)`; both are bundled in one existential because the isomorphism is an isomorphism *over*
`φ`. Only the algebra structure of `D⟨ξ_i(j)⟩` enters, which is what "of algebras over `D`"
asks for, so the divided powers of `D` itself are not needed to state the lemma.

The `(n + 1)`-fold tensor power is the polynomial algebra on `Fin (n + 1) × ι` as in the
construction of `D(n)`, the coprojection `h ↦ h ⊗ 1 ⊗ … ⊗ 1` is renaming along `i ↦ (0, i)`,
and `ξ_i(j) = x_{(0, i)} - x_{(j + 1, i)}`. The variables `ξ_i(j)` are indexed by `ι × Fin n`,
the index `j : Fin n` standing for the slot `j + 1` as in the source, where `j` runs over
`1, …, n`.

The proof changes coordinates on the tensor power, writing it as the polynomial algebra over
its first factor on the variables `ξ_i(j)` and carrying `J(n)` to the ideal generated by `J`
and the variables, and then identifies the divided power envelope using the lemma on adjoining
variables. That lemma is available in the library only when the ring and the variables lie in
the universe of the divided power base, while here they lie in the universe of the polynomial
algebra, so its universal-property argument is repeated at independent universes. Passing from
the uncompleted identification to the completed one uses that the divided power polynomial
algebra is free on the divided power monomials, so that reducing coefficients modulo `p^e`
commutes with forming it.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Lemma 60.17.5, Tag 07L2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07L2)
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u v w

namespace Crystalline

open DividedPowers

variable (s : AffineCrystallineSituation.{u, v})

variable {ι : Type w} (f : MvPolynomial ι s.A →ₐ[s.A] s.C) (hf : Function.Surjective f)

/-! ### The ideal `(p)` and its completions -/

/-- The ideal generated by the fixed prime, in which all completions below are taken. -/
private abbrev pIdeal (R : Type*) [CommRing R] (p : ℕ) : Ideal R :=
  Ideal.span {(p : R)}

/-! ### The elements `ξ_i(j)` -/

/-- The element `ξ_i(j) = x_i ⊗ 1 ⊗ … ⊗ 1 - 1 ⊗ … ⊗ 1 ⊗ x_i ⊗ 1 ⊗ … ⊗ 1` of
`P ⊗_A … ⊗_A P`, the second `x_i` sitting in the `(j + 1)`-st slot.  The variables are
indexed by `q : ι × Fin n`, with `i = q.1` and `j = q.2 + 1`, so that `j` runs over
`1, …, n` as in the source; the `(j + 1)`-st slot is then the factor with index
`q.2.succ = j` of the `n + 1` factors indexed by `Fin (n + 1)`, the first factor having
index `0`. -/
public noncomputable def coprojectionDifference (n : ℕ) (q : ι × Fin n) :
    MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1) × ι) s.A :=
  MvPolynomial.X ((0 : Fin (n + 1)), q.1) - MvPolynomial.X ((q.2.succ : Fin (n + 1)), q.1)

private theorem sub_constantCoeff_mem_variables {R : Type*} [CommRing R]
    (W : Type*) (p : MvPolynomial W R) :
    p - MvPolynomial.C (MvPolynomial.constantCoeff p) ∈
      Ideal.span (Set.range (MvPolynomial.X : W → MvPolynomial W R)) := by
  classical
  induction p using MvPolynomial.induction_on with
  | C r => simp
  | add p q hp hq =>
      have hrewrite : p + q - MvPolynomial.C (MvPolynomial.constantCoeff (p + q)) =
          (p - MvPolynomial.C (MvPolynomial.constantCoeff p)) +
            (q - MvPolynomial.C (MvPolynomial.constantCoeff q)) := by
        simp only [map_add]
        ring
      rw [hrewrite]
      exact add_mem hp hq
  | mul_X p i hp =>
      simp only [map_mul, MvPolynomial.constantCoeff_X, mul_zero,
        map_zero, sub_zero]
      have hx : MvPolynomial.X i ∈
          Ideal.span (Set.range (MvPolynomial.X : W → MvPolynomial W R)) :=
        Ideal.subset_span (show MvPolynomial.X i ∈
          Set.range (MvPolynomial.X : W → MvPolynomial W R) from ⟨i, rfl⟩)
      simpa [mul_comm] using Ideal.mul_mem_right (b := p) _ hx

private theorem ker_eval₂Hom_zero {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    (f : R →+* S) (W : Type*) :
    RingHom.ker (MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom f (0 : W → S)) =
      (RingHom.ker f).map MvPolynomial.C +
        Ideal.span (Set.range (MvPolynomial.X : W → MvPolynomial W R)) := by
  classical
  ext p
  constructor
  · intro hp
    have hconst : f (MvPolynomial.constantCoeff p) = 0 := by
      simpa [MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom_zero_apply] using hp
    have hcoeff : MvPolynomial.C (MvPolynomial.constantCoeff p) ∈
        (RingHom.ker f).map MvPolynomial.C :=
      Ideal.mem_map_of_mem (MvPolynomial.C : R →+* MvPolynomial W R) hconst
    have hvars := sub_constantCoeff_mem_variables W p
    have hdecomp : p = MvPolynomial.C (MvPolynomial.constantCoeff p) +
        (p - MvPolynomial.C (MvPolynomial.constantCoeff p)) := by ring
    rw [hdecomp]
    exact add_mem (Ideal.mem_sup_left hcoeff) (Ideal.mem_sup_right hvars)
  · intro hp
    rw [Ideal.add_eq_sup] at hp
    rcases Submodule.mem_sup.mp hp with ⟨a, ha, b, hb, hab⟩
    have hca : MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom f (0 : W → S) a = 0 := by
      rw [MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom_zero_apply]
      have ha' : a ∈ RingHom.ker (MvPolynomial.map f) := by
        rw [MvPolynomial.ker_map]
        exact ha
      have hamap : MvPolynomial.map f a = 0 := RingHom.mem_ker.mp ha'
      have := congrArg MvPolynomial.constantCoeff hamap
      simpa [MvPolynomial.constantCoeff_map] using this
    have hxb : MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom f (0 : W → S) b = 0 := by
      refine Submodule.span_induction (p := fun x _ =>
        MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom f (0 : W → S) x = 0) ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ hb
      · intro x hx
        rcases Set.mem_range.mp hx with ⟨i, rfl⟩
        simp
      · simp
      · intro x y _ _ hx hy
        rw [MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom_zero_apply] at hx hy ⊢
        simpa using congrArg₂ (· + ·) hx hy
      · intro c x _ hx
        rw [MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom_zero_apply] at hx ⊢
        simpa using congrArg (fun z : S => f (MvPolynomial.constantCoeff c) * z) hx
    apply RingHom.mem_ker.mpr
    rw [← hab, map_add, hca, hxb, add_zero]

private abbrev liftedDifferenceIndex (n : ℕ) := ULift.{max u w, w} (ι × Fin n)

private def differenceIndexEquiv (n : ℕ) :
    Fin (n + 1) × ι ≃ liftedDifferenceIndex (ι := ι) n ⊕ ι where
  toFun q := Fin.cases (Sum.inr q.2) (fun j => Sum.inl (ULift.up (q.2, j))) q.1
  invFun := Sum.elim (fun q => (q.down.2.succ, q.down.1)) (fun i => (0, i))
  left_inv := by
    rintro ⟨j, i⟩
    cases j using Fin.cases <;> rfl
  right_inv := by
    intro q
    cases q with
    | inl q => cases q with | up q => cases q; rfl
    | inr i => rfl

private noncomputable def differenceShiftHom (n : ℕ) :
    MvPolynomial (liftedDifferenceIndex (ι := ι) n) (MvPolynomial ι s.A) →+*
      MvPolynomial (liftedDifferenceIndex (ι := ι) n) (MvPolynomial ι s.A) :=
  (MvPolynomial.aeval (fun q : liftedDifferenceIndex (ι := ι) n =>
    MvPolynomial.C (MvPolynomial.X q.down.1) - MvPolynomial.X q)).toRingHom

private theorem differenceShiftHom_involutive (n : ℕ)
    (p : MvPolynomial (liftedDifferenceIndex (ι := ι) n) (MvPolynomial ι s.A)) :
    differenceShiftHom s n (differenceShiftHom s n p) = p := by
  induction p using MvPolynomial.induction_on with
  | C a => simp [differenceShiftHom]
  | add p q hp hq => simp [map_add, hp, hq]
  | mul_X p q hp =>
      have hX : differenceShiftHom s n
          (differenceShiftHom s n (MvPolynomial.X q)) = MvPolynomial.X q := by
        simp [differenceShiftHom]
      rw [map_mul, map_mul, hp, hX]

private noncomputable def differenceShiftEquiv (n : ℕ) :
    MvPolynomial (liftedDifferenceIndex (ι := ι) n) (MvPolynomial ι s.A) ≃+*
      MvPolynomial (liftedDifferenceIndex (ι := ι) n) (MvPolynomial ι s.A) :=
  RingEquiv.ofBijective (differenceShiftHom s n)
    (Function.Involutive.bijective (differenceShiftHom_involutive s n))

private noncomputable def tensorDifferenceCoordinates (n : ℕ) :
    MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1) × ι) s.A ≃+*
      MvPolynomial (liftedDifferenceIndex (ι := ι) n) (MvPolynomial ι s.A) := by
  let e₁ := MvPolynomial.renameEquiv s.A (differenceIndexEquiv (ι := ι) n)
  let e₂ := MvPolynomial.sumAlgEquiv s.A (liftedDifferenceIndex (ι := ι) n) ι
  exact (e₁.trans e₂).toRingEquiv.trans (differenceShiftEquiv s n)

private theorem tensorDifferenceCoordinates_X_zero (n : ℕ) (i : ι) :
    tensorDifferenceCoordinates s n (MvPolynomial.X ((0 : Fin (n + 1)), i)) =
      MvPolynomial.C (MvPolynomial.X i) := by
  simp [tensorDifferenceCoordinates, differenceIndexEquiv,
    differenceShiftEquiv, differenceShiftHom]

private theorem tensorDifferenceCoordinates_X_succ (n : ℕ) (i : ι) (j : Fin n) :
    tensorDifferenceCoordinates s n (MvPolynomial.X (j.succ, i)) =
      MvPolynomial.C (MvPolynomial.X i) - MvPolynomial.X (ULift.up (i, j)) := by
  simp [tensorDifferenceCoordinates, differenceIndexEquiv,
    differenceShiftEquiv, differenceShiftHom]

private theorem tensorDifferenceCoordinates_coprojectionDifference (n : ℕ) (q : ι × Fin n) :
    tensorDifferenceCoordinates s n (coprojectionDifference s n q) =
      MvPolynomial.X (ULift.up q) := by
  rw [coprojectionDifference, map_sub, tensorDifferenceCoordinates_X_zero,
    tensorDifferenceCoordinates_X_succ]
  ring

private theorem tensorDifferenceCoordinates_coprojection (n : ℕ) (x : MvPolynomial ι s.A) :
    tensorDifferenceCoordinates s n (mvPolynomialCoprojection s.A (0 : Fin (n + 1)) x) =
      MvPolynomial.C x := by
  have h : (tensorDifferenceCoordinates s n).toRingHom.comp
      (mvPolynomialCoprojection s.A (0 : Fin (n + 1))).toRingHom =
      (MvPolynomial.C : MvPolynomial ι s.A →+*
        MvPolynomial (liftedDifferenceIndex (ι := ι) n) (MvPolynomial ι s.A)) := by
    apply MvPolynomial.ringHom_ext <;> intro <;>
      simp [tensorDifferenceCoordinates, differenceIndexEquiv, differenceShiftEquiv,
        differenceShiftHom, mvPolynomialCoprojection]
  exact RingHom.congr_fun h x

private noncomputable def differenceCoordinateEvaluation (n : ℕ) :
    MvPolynomial (liftedDifferenceIndex (ι := ι) n) (MvPolynomial ι s.A) →+* s.C :=
  MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom f.toRingHom (0 : liftedDifferenceIndex (ι := ι) n → s.C)

private theorem differenceCoordinateEvaluation_comp (n : ℕ) :
    (differenceCoordinateEvaluation s f n).comp
        (tensorDifferenceCoordinates s n).toRingHom =
      (tensorPowerPresentation s f n).toRingHom := by
  apply MvPolynomial.ringHom_ext
  · intro a
    simp [differenceCoordinateEvaluation, tensorDifferenceCoordinates,
      differenceIndexEquiv, differenceShiftEquiv, differenceShiftHom,
      tensorPowerPresentation]
  · intro q
    rcases q with ⟨k, i⟩
    cases k using Fin.cases with
    | zero =>
        simp [differenceCoordinateEvaluation, tensorDifferenceCoordinates_X_zero,
          tensorPowerPresentation]
    | succ j =>
        simp [differenceCoordinateEvaluation, tensorDifferenceCoordinates_X_succ,
          tensorPowerPresentation]

private theorem tensorKernel_map_differenceCoordinates (n : ℕ) :
    Ideal.map (tensorDifferenceCoordinates s n).toRingHom
      (RingHom.ker (tensorPowerPresentation s f n).toRingHom) =
      polynomialEnvelopeIdeal (RingHom.ker f.toRingHom)
        (liftedDifferenceIndex (ι := ι) n) := by
  rw [← differenceCoordinateEvaluation_comp]
  rw [← RingHom.comap_ker]
  rw [Ideal.map_comap_of_surjective (tensorDifferenceCoordinates s n).toRingHom
    (tensorDifferenceCoordinates s n).surjective]
  unfold differenceCoordinateEvaluation polynomialEnvelopeIdeal
  rw [ker_eval₂Hom_zero]

private noncomputable def dividedPowerPolynomialIndexEquiv (n : ℕ)
    (D : DividedPowerRing.{max u w}) :
    setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialAlgebra D (liftedDifferenceIndex (ι := ι) n) ≃ₐ[D]
      setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialAlgebra D (ι × Fin n) := by
  let down : liftedDifferenceIndex (ι := ι) n → ι × Fin n := ULift.down
  let up : (ι × Fin n) → liftedDifferenceIndex (ι := ι) n := ULift.up
  let fwd := DividedPowerAlgebra.map D
    (Finsupp.lmapDomain D D down)
  let bwd := DividedPowerAlgebra.map D
    (Finsupp.lmapDomain D D up)
  have hl₁ : (Finsupp.lmapDomain D D down).comp
      (Finsupp.lmapDomain D D up) = LinearMap.id := by
    rw [← Finsupp.lmapDomain_comp, show down ∘ up = id by funext x; rfl, Finsupp.lmapDomain_id]
  have hl₂ : (Finsupp.lmapDomain D D up).comp
      (Finsupp.lmapDomain D D down) = LinearMap.id := by
    rw [← Finsupp.lmapDomain_comp, show up ∘ down = id by funext x; cases x with | up y => rfl,
      Finsupp.lmapDomain_id]
  have h₁ : fwd.comp bwd = AlgHom.id D _ := by
    calc
      fwd.comp bwd = DividedPowerAlgebra.map D
          ((Finsupp.lmapDomain D D down).comp (Finsupp.lmapDomain D D up)) := by
            rw [← DividedPowerAlgebra.map_comp]
      _ = DividedPowerAlgebra.map D LinearMap.id := by rw [hl₁]
      _ = AlgHom.id D _ := DividedPowerAlgebra.map_id
  have h₂ : bwd.comp fwd = AlgHom.id D _ := by
    calc
      bwd.comp fwd = DividedPowerAlgebra.map D
          ((Finsupp.lmapDomain D D up).comp (Finsupp.lmapDomain D D down)) := by
            rw [← DividedPowerAlgebra.map_comp]
      _ = DividedPowerAlgebra.map D LinearMap.id := by rw [hl₂]
      _ = AlgHom.id D _ := DividedPowerAlgebra.map_id
  apply AlgEquiv.ofBijective fwd
  constructor
  · intro x y hxy
    have h := congrArg bwd hxy
    change (bwd.comp fwd) x = (bwd.comp fwd) y at h
    rw [h₂] at h
    exact h
  · intro y
    refine ⟨bwd y, ?_⟩
    have h := congrArg (fun g : _ →ₐ[D] _ => g y) h₁
    simpa only [AlgHom.comp_apply, AlgHom.id_apply] using h


private alias basePolynomialIdeal_le_kernel := ideal_map_le_ker_presentation

private theorem adicCompletionMap_comp' {R S T : Type*}
    [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [CommRing T]
    (f : R →+* S) (g : S →+* T) (I : Ideal R) (J : Ideal S) (K : Ideal T)
    (hf : I.map f ≤ J) (hg : J.map g ≤ K) :
    (adicCompletionMap g J K hg).comp (adicCompletionMap f I J hf) =
      adicCompletionMap (g.comp f) I K
        (by rw [← Ideal.map_map]; exact (Ideal.map_mono hf).trans hg) := by
  apply RingHom.ext
  intro x
  apply AdicCompletion.ext_evalₐ
  intro n
  simp only [RingHom.comp_apply, adicCompletionMap_evalₐ]
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective (AdicCompletion.evalₐ I n x)
  rw [← hy]
  rfl

private theorem pIdeal_map_le {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    (g : R →+* S) (p : ℕ) : (pIdeal R p).map g ≤ pIdeal S p := by
  simp [pIdeal, Ideal.map_span]

private noncomputable def pAdicCompletionEquiv {R S : Type*}
    [CommRing R] [CommRing S] (e : R ≃+* S) (p : ℕ) :
    AdicCompletion (Ideal.span {(p : R)}) R ≃+*
      AdicCompletion (Ideal.span {(p : S)}) S := by
  let I : Ideal R := Ideal.span {(p : R)}
  let J : Ideal S := Ideal.span {(p : S)}
  exact RingEquiv.ofRingHom
    (adicCompletionMap e.toRingHom I J (pIdeal_map_le e.toRingHom p))
    (adicCompletionMap e.symm.toRingHom J I (pIdeal_map_le e.symm.toRingHom p))
    (by
      rw [adicCompletionMap_comp']
      simpa using _root_.completionMapOfRingHom_id J (by simp))
    (by
      rw [adicCompletionMap_comp']
      simpa using _root_.completionMapOfRingHom_id I (by simp))

/-- The divided power morphism out of an envelope classified by a morphism of pairs out of
`(B, J)` restricts to that morphism along the canonical map from `B`. -/
private theorem DividedPowerEnvelope.homEquiv_symm_comp_algebraMap
    {A : DividedPowerRing.{u}} {B : Type v} [CommRing B] {f : A →+* B} {J : Ideal B}
    {hJ : A.ideal.map f ≤ J} (D : DividedPowerEnvelope A f J hJ)
    (C : DividedPowerRing.{max u v})
    (a : DividedPowers.DPMorphism A.dividedPowers C.dividedPowers) (φ : B →+* C.carrier)
    (hφ : J.map φ ≤ C.ideal)
    (h : IdealPair.Hom.comp (IdealPair.Hom.ofRingHom φ hφ) (IdealPair.Hom.ofRingHom f hJ) =
      IdealPair.Hom.ofDPMorphism a) :
    ((D.homEquiv C a).symm ⟨_, h⟩).1.toRingHom.comp D.algebraMap.toRingHom = φ := by
  have hr := congrArg IdealPair.Hom.toRingHom
    ((congrArg Subtype.val ((D.homEquiv C a).apply_symm_apply ⟨_, h⟩)).symm.trans
      (D.homEquiv_apply C a _))
  simpa [IdealPair.Hom.ofRingHom, IdealPair.Hom.comp, IdealPair.Hom.ofDPMorphism] using hr.symm

/-- Ring maps intertwining two algebra maps along `e` and `e.symm` compose to the identity on
the base. -/
private theorem comp_comp_eq_of_intertwine {B C X Y : Type*} [CommRing B] [CommRing C]
    [CommRing X] [CommRing Y] (e : B ≃+* C) (aX : B →+* X) (aY : C →+* Y) (q : X →+* Y)
    (r : Y →+* X) (hq : q.comp aX = aY.comp e.toRingHom)
    (hr : r.comp aY = aX.comp e.symm.toRingHom) : (r.comp q).comp aX = aX := by
  rw [RingHom.comp_assoc, hq, ← RingHom.comp_assoc, hr, RingHom.comp_assoc]
  ext x
  simp

private theorem dividedPowerEnvelopeMapOfPresentationEquiv
    {A : DividedPowerRing.{u}} {B C : Type v}
    [CommRing B] [CommRing C]
    (f : A →+* B) (J : Ideal B) (hf : A.ideal.map f ≤ J)
    (g : A →+* C) (K : Ideal C) (hg : A.ideal.map g ≤ K)
    (e : B ≃+* C) (he : e.toRingHom.comp f = g)
    (hJ : Ideal.map e.toRingHom J ≤ K)
    (D : DividedPowerEnvelope A f J hf)
    (E : DividedPowerEnvelope A g K hg) :
    ∃ q : D.object.dividedPowers.DPMorphism E.object.dividedPowers,
      q.comp D.structureMap = E.structureMap ∧
        q.toRingHom.comp D.algebraMap.toRingHom =
          E.algebraMap.toRingHom.comp e.toRingHom := by
  let pair : IdealPair.Hom J E.object.ideal := IdealPair.Hom.ofRingHom
    (E.algebraMap.toRingHom.comp e.toRingHom) (by
      calc
        Ideal.map (E.algebraMap.toRingHom.comp e.toRingHom) J =
            (Ideal.map e.toRingHom J).map E.algebraMap.toRingHom := by
              rw [← Ideal.map_map]
        _ ≤ E.object.ideal := (Ideal.map_mono hJ).trans E.algebraMap.ideal_comp)
  have hover : IdealPair.Hom.comp pair (IdealPair.Hom.ofRingHom f hf) =
      IdealPair.Hom.ofDPMorphism E.structureMap := by
    apply IdealPair.Hom.ext_toRingHom
    change (E.algebraMap.toRingHom.comp e.toRingHom).comp f = E.structureMap.toRingHom
    rw [RingHom.comp_assoc, he, E.algebraMap_comp]
  let data := (D.homEquiv E.object E.structureMap).symm ⟨pair, hover⟩
  exact ⟨data.1, data.2, D.homEquiv_symm_comp_algebraMap E.object E.structureMap _ _ hover⟩

/-- **Two divided power envelopes of corresponding ideals under an isomorphism of presentations
are isomorphic as divided power rings.**

The isomorphism is produced by the universal property of each envelope applied to the other, so
it is a divided power morphism in *both* directions and commutes with the two structure maps
from the divided power base.  Those three clauses are what carry the isomorphism through the
divided power differentials; a bare ring isomorphism identifies the two rings and nothing of
their divided power structure. -/
public theorem dividedPowerEnvelopeEquivOfPresentationEquiv
    {A : DividedPowerRing.{u}} {B C : Type v}
    [CommRing B] [CommRing C]
    (f : A →+* B) (J : Ideal B) (hf : A.ideal.map f ≤ J)
    (g : A →+* C) (K : Ideal C) (hg : A.ideal.map g ≤ K)
    (e : B ≃+* C) (he : e.toRingHom.comp f = g)
    (hJ : Ideal.map e.toRingHom J ≤ K)
    (hK : Ideal.map e.symm.toRingHom K ≤ J)
    (D : DividedPowerEnvelope A f J hf)
    (E : DividedPowerEnvelope A g K hg) :
    ∃ qEquiv : D.object.carrier ≃+* E.object.carrier,
      qEquiv.toRingHom.comp D.algebraMap.toRingHom =
          E.algebraMap.toRingHom.comp e.toRingHom ∧
        DividedPowers.IsDPMorphism D.object.dividedPowers E.object.dividedPowers
          qEquiv.toRingHom ∧
        DividedPowers.IsDPMorphism E.object.dividedPowers D.object.dividedPowers
          qEquiv.symm.toRingHom ∧
        qEquiv.toRingHom.comp D.structureMap.toRingHom = E.structureMap.toRingHom := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨q, hqA, hqB⟩ := dividedPowerEnvelopeMapOfPresentationEquiv f J hf g K hg e he hJ D E
  have hesymm : e.symm.toRingHom.comp g = f := by
    rw [← he]
    ext x
    simp
  obtain ⟨r, hrA, hrB⟩ := dividedPowerEnvelopeMapOfPresentationEquiv
    g K hg f J hf e.symm hesymm hK E D
  have hqrBase : (r.comp q).toRingHom.comp D.algebraMap.toRingHom =
      D.algebraMap.toRingHom :=
    comp_comp_eq_of_intertwine e _ _ _ _ hqB hrB
  have hqr : r.comp q = DividedPowers.DPMorphism.id D.object.dividedPowers :=
    envelopeHom_ext D D.object (r.comp q) (DividedPowers.DPMorphism.id _)
      ((congrArg (r.comp ·) hqA).trans hrA) hqrBase
  have hbaseqr : (q.comp r).toRingHom.comp E.algebraMap.toRingHom =
      E.algebraMap.toRingHom :=
    comp_comp_eq_of_intertwine e.symm _ _ _ _ hrB hqB
  have hqr' : q.comp r = DividedPowers.DPMorphism.id E.object.dividedPowers :=
    envelopeHom_ext E E.object (q.comp r) (DividedPowers.DPMorphism.id _)
      ((congrArg (q.comp ·) hrA).trans hqA) hbaseqr
  let eRing := RingEquiv.ofRingHom q.toRingHom r.toRingHom
    (RingHom.ext fun x => congrArg (fun z => z x) hqr')
    (RingHom.ext fun x => congrArg (fun z => z x) hqr)
  exact ⟨eRing, hqB, q.isDPMorphism, r.isDPMorphism,
    congrArg DividedPowers.DPMorphism.toRingHom hqA⟩

/-! ### Adjoining variables to a divided power envelope, with the variables in the universe of
the ring rather than that of the divided power base -/

/-- The image of the base divided power ideal lies in the polynomial envelope ideal, for a ring
and a type of variables in a universe independent of that of the divided power base. -/
public lemma baseIdeal_le_polynomialEnvelopeIdeal'
    {A : DividedPowerRing.{u}} {B : Type v} [CommRing B] (f : A →+* B) (J : Ideal B)
    (hJ : A.ideal.map f ≤ J) (W : Type v) :
    A.ideal.map (MvPolynomial.C.comp f) ≤ polynomialEnvelopeIdeal J W := by
  calc
    A.ideal.map (MvPolynomial.C.comp f) = (A.ideal.map f).map MvPolynomial.C := by
      rw [Ideal.map_map]
    _ ≤ J.map MvPolynomial.C := Ideal.map_mono hJ
    _ ≤ polynomialEnvelopeIdeal J W := le_sup_left

/-- The evaluation of polynomials over `B` in the divided power polynomial algebra over an
envelope of `(B, J)`, sending the variables to the divided power variables, carries the ideal
generated by `J` and the variables into the divided power ideal. -/
private theorem DividedPowerEnvelope.map_polynomialEnvelopeIdeal_le
    {A : DividedPowerRing.{u}} {B : Type v} [CommRing B] {f : A →+* B} {J : Ideal B}
    {hJ : A.ideal.map f ≤ J} (D : DividedPowerEnvelope A f J hJ) (W : Type v) :
    (polynomialEnvelopeIdeal J W).map (MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom
        ((setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialCoefficientDPMorphism D.object W).toRingHom.comp
          D.algebraMap.toRingHom) fun i => dividedPowerPolynomialVariable D.object i) ≤
      dividedPowerPolynomialIdeal D.object.ideal W := by
  change Ideal.map _ (J.map MvPolynomial.C + Ideal.span (Set.range MvPolynomial.X)) ≤ _
  rw [Ideal.add_eq_sup, Ideal.map_sup, Ideal.map_map]
  refine sup_le (Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr fun b hb => ?_)
    (Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr (Ideal.span_le.2 ?_))
  · rw [Ideal.mem_comap, RingHom.comp_apply, MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom_C]
    exact (setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialCoefficientDPMorphism D.object W).ideal_comp
      (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ (D.algebraMap.ideal_comp (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ hb)))
  · rintro _ ⟨i, rfl⟩
    rw [SetLike.mem_coe, Ideal.mem_comap, MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom_X']
    exact variable_mem_polynomialIdeal D.object i

/-- The divided power morphism from the envelope of `(B[W], J B[W] + (W))` to the divided power
polynomial algebra over the envelope of `(B, J)` which extends the evaluation at the divided
power variables. -/
private theorem DividedPowerEnvelope.exists_dpMorphism_toDividedPowerPolynomial
    {A : DividedPowerRing.{u}} {B : Type v} [CommRing B] {f : A →+* B} {J : Ideal B}
    {hJ : A.ideal.map f ≤ J} {W : Type v} (D : DividedPowerEnvelope A f J hJ)
    (E : DividedPowerEnvelope A (MvPolynomial.C.comp f)
      (polynomialEnvelopeIdeal J W) (baseIdeal_le_polynomialEnvelopeIdeal' f J hJ W)) :
    ∃ q : E.object.dividedPowers.DPMorphism
        (setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialDividedPowers D.object W),
      q.comp E.structureMap =
          (setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialCoefficientDPMorphism D.object W).comp
            D.structureMap ∧
        q.toRingHom.comp E.algebraMap.toRingHom = MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom
          ((setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialCoefficientDPMorphism D.object W).toRingHom.comp
            D.algebraMap.toRingHom) fun i => dividedPowerPolynomialVariable D.object i := by
  let coeff := setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialCoefficientDPMorphism D.object W
  let Pdp : DividedPowerRing := .of (setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialAlgebra D.object W)
    (dividedPowerPolynomialIdeal D.object.ideal W)
    (setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialDividedPowers D.object W)
  have hbase : IdealPair.Hom.comp
      (IdealPair.Hom.ofRingHom _ (D.map_polynomialEnvelopeIdeal_le W))
      (IdealPair.Hom.ofRingHom (MvPolynomial.C.comp f)
        (baseIdeal_le_polynomialEnvelopeIdeal' f J hJ W)) =
      IdealPair.Hom.ofDPMorphism (coeff.comp D.structureMap) := by
    apply IdealPair.Hom.ext_toRingHom
    ext a
    change MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom _ _ (MvPolynomial.C (f a)) = coeff (D.structureMap a)
    rw [MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom_C]
    exact congrArg (fun g : A →+* D.object.carrier => coeff (g a)) D.algebraMap_comp
  exact ⟨((E.homEquiv Pdp (coeff.comp D.structureMap)).symm ⟨_, hbase⟩).1,
    ((E.homEquiv Pdp (coeff.comp D.structureMap)).symm ⟨_, hbase⟩).2,
    E.homEquiv_symm_comp_algebraMap Pdp (coeff.comp D.structureMap) _ _ hbase⟩

/-- The divided power morphism from the divided power polynomial algebra over the envelope of
`(B, J)` to the envelope of `(B[W], J B[W] + (W))` which sends the divided power variables to
the variables. -/
private theorem DividedPowerEnvelope.exists_dpMorphism_ofDividedPowerPolynomial
    {A : DividedPowerRing.{u}} {B : Type v} [CommRing B] {f : A →+* B} {J : Ideal B}
    {hJ : A.ideal.map f ≤ J} {W : Type v} (D : DividedPowerEnvelope A f J hJ)
    (E : DividedPowerEnvelope A (MvPolynomial.C.comp f)
      (polynomialEnvelopeIdeal J W) (baseIdeal_le_polynomialEnvelopeIdeal' f J hJ W)) :
    ∃ p : (setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialDividedPowers D.object W).DPMorphism
        E.object.dividedPowers,
      (p.comp (setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialCoefficientDPMorphism D.object W)).comp
          D.structureMap = E.structureMap ∧
        (p.comp (setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialCoefficientDPMorphism D.object W)).toRingHom.comp
          D.algebraMap.toRingHom = E.algebraMap.toRingHom.comp MvPolynomial.C ∧
        ∀ i : W, p (dividedPowerPolynomialVariable D.object i) =
          E.algebraMap.toRingHom (MvPolynomial.X i) := by
  have hJE : J.map (E.algebraMap.toRingHom.comp MvPolynomial.C) ≤ E.object.ideal := by
    rw [← Ideal.map_map]
    exact (Ideal.map_mono (le_sup_left :
      J.map MvPolynomial.C ≤ polynomialEnvelopeIdeal J W)).trans E.algebraMap.ideal_comp
  have hover : IdealPair.Hom.comp (IdealPair.Hom.ofRingHom _ hJE) (IdealPair.Hom.ofRingHom f hJ) =
      IdealPair.Hom.ofDPMorphism E.structureMap := by
    apply IdealPair.Hom.ext_toRingHom
    ext a
    change E.algebraMap.toRingHom (MvPolynomial.C (f a)) = E.structureMap a
    exact congrArg (fun g : A →+* E.object.carrier => g a) E.algebraMap_comp
  have hX (i : W) : E.algebraMap.toRingHom (MvPolynomial.X i) ∈ E.object.ideal :=
    E.algebraMap.ideal_comp (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _
      (show MvPolynomial.X i ∈ polynomialEnvelopeIdeal J W from
        Ideal.mem_sup_right (Ideal.subset_span ⟨i, rfl⟩)))
  let d := (D.homEquiv E.object E.structureMap).symm ⟨_, hover⟩
  obtain ⟨p, hp, hpX⟩ := (existsUnique_dPMorphism_from_setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomial
    D.object W E.object d.1 fun i => ⟨_, hX i⟩).exists
  refine ⟨p, by rw [hp]; exact d.2, ?_, hpX⟩
  rw [hp]
  exact D.homEquiv_symm_comp_algebraMap _ _ _ _ hover

/-- The divided power envelope of a polynomial algebra along the extended ideal and the
variables is canonically the divided power polynomial algebra over the original envelope.  This
is `Crystalline.dividedPowerEnvelopeAddVariables` with the ring and the variables in a universe
independent of that of the divided power base, which is the generality needed when the base is
`(A, I, γ)` and the ring is a polynomial algebra over `A` on variables in a larger universe; the
proof is the same two applications of the universal properties. -/
public theorem dividedPowerEnvelopeAddVariables'
    {A : DividedPowerRing.{u}} {B : Type v} [CommRing B] (f : A →+* B) (J : Ideal B)
    (hJ : A.ideal.map f ≤ J) (W : Type v)
    (D : DividedPowerEnvelope A f J hJ)
    (E : DividedPowerEnvelope A (MvPolynomial.C.comp f)
      (polynomialEnvelopeIdeal J W) (baseIdeal_le_polynomialEnvelopeIdeal' f J hJ W)) :
    ∃ e : E.object ≃+* setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialAlgebra D.object W,
      DividedPowers.IsDPMorphism E.object.dividedPowers
        (setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialDividedPowers D.object W) e.toRingHom ∧
      DividedPowers.IsDPMorphism
        (setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialDividedPowers D.object W)
        E.object.dividedPowers e.symm.toRingHom ∧
      (∀ b : B, e (E.algebraMap.toRingHom (MvPolynomial.C b)) =
        algebraMap D.object (setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialAlgebra D.object W)
          (D.algebraMap.toRingHom b)) ∧
      (∀ i : W, e (E.algebraMap.toRingHom (MvPolynomial.X i)) =
        dividedPowerPolynomialVariable D.object i) := by
  obtain ⟨eDP, heA, heB⟩ := D.exists_dpMorphism_toDividedPowerPolynomial E
  obtain ⟨pDP, hpA, hpB, hpX⟩ := D.exists_dpMorphism_ofDividedPowerPolynomial E
  set coeff := setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialCoefficientDPMorphism D.object W
  let Pdp : DividedPowerRing := .of (setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialAlgebra D.object W)
    (dividedPowerPolynomialIdeal D.object.ideal W)
    (setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialDividedPowers D.object W)
  have hCompCoeff : (eDP.comp pDP).comp coeff = coeff := by
    refine envelopeHom_ext D Pdp ((eDP.comp pDP).comp coeff) coeff
      ((congrArg (eDP.comp ·) hpA).trans heA) ?_
    calc ((eDP.comp pDP).comp coeff).toRingHom.comp D.algebraMap.toRingHom
        = eDP.toRingHom.comp ((pDP.comp coeff).toRingHom.comp D.algebraMap.toRingHom) := rfl
      _ = (eDP.toRingHom.comp E.algebraMap.toRingHom).comp MvPolynomial.C := by
        rw [hpB, RingHom.comp_assoc]
      _ = coeff.toRingHom.comp D.algebraMap.toRingHom := by
        rw [heB, MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom_comp_C]
  have hCompVar (i : W) : (eDP.comp pDP) (dividedPowerPolynomialVariable D.object i) =
      dividedPowerPolynomialVariable D.object i := by
    change eDP (pDP _) = _
    rw [hpX]
    exact (RingHom.congr_fun heB _).trans (MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom_X' _ _ i)
  have hCompP : eDP.comp pDP = DividedPowers.DPMorphism.id
      (setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialDividedPowers D.object W) :=
    (existsUnique_dPMorphism_from_setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomial D.object W Pdp coeff
      fun i => ⟨_, variable_mem_polynomialIdeal D.object i⟩).unique (y₁ := eDP.comp pDP)
      (y₂ := DividedPowers.DPMorphism.id
        (setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialDividedPowers D.object W))
      ⟨hCompCoeff, hCompVar⟩ ⟨rfl, fun _ => rfl⟩
  have hCompE : pDP.comp eDP = DividedPowers.DPMorphism.id E.object.dividedPowers := by
    refine envelopeHom_ext E E.object (pDP.comp eDP)
      (DividedPowers.DPMorphism.id E.object.dividedPowers)
      ((congrArg (pDP.comp ·) heA).trans hpA) ?_
    have hP : pDP.toRingHom.comp (MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom
        (coeff.toRingHom.comp D.algebraMap.toRingHom)
          fun i => dividedPowerPolynomialVariable D.object i) = E.algebraMap.toRingHom :=
      MvPolynomial.ringHom_ext'
        (by rw [RingHom.comp_assoc, MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom_comp_C]; exact hpB) fun i => by
          rw [RingHom.comp_apply, MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom_X']; exact hpX i
    change pDP.toRingHom.comp (eDP.toRingHom.comp E.algebraMap.toRingHom) = E.algebraMap.toRingHom
    rw [heB, hP]
  have hRingInvP : eDP.toRingHom.comp pDP.toRingHom =
      RingHom.id (setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialAlgebra D.object W) :=
    RingHom.ext fun x => congrArg (fun q => q x) hCompP
  have hRingInvE : pDP.toRingHom.comp eDP.toRingHom = RingHom.id E.object.carrier :=
    RingHom.ext fun x => congrArg (fun q => q x) hCompE
  let e : E.object.carrier ≃+* setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialAlgebra D.object W :=
    RingEquiv.ofRingHom eDP.toRingHom pDP.toRingHom hRingInvP hRingInvE
  have he : e.toRingHom = eDP.toRingHom := by
    ext x
    exact RingEquiv.ofRingHom_apply eDP.toRingHom pDP.toRingHom hRingInvP hRingInvE x
  refine ⟨e, ?_, ?_, fun b => ?_, fun i => ?_⟩
  · rw [he]
    exact eDP.isDPMorphism
  · change DividedPowers.IsDPMorphism
      (setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialDividedPowers D.object W)
      E.object.dividedPowers pDP.toRingHom
    exact pDP.isDPMorphism
  · change eDP.toRingHom (E.algebraMap.toRingHom (MvPolynomial.C b)) = _
    calc
      eDP.toRingHom (E.algebraMap.toRingHom (MvPolynomial.C b)) =
          MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom (coeff.toRingHom.comp D.algebraMap.toRingHom)
            (fun i => dividedPowerPolynomialVariable D.object i) (MvPolynomial.C b) :=
        RingHom.congr_fun heB _
      _ = coeff.toRingHom (D.algebraMap.toRingHom b) := by simp
  · change eDP.toRingHom (E.algebraMap.toRingHom (MvPolynomial.X i)) = _
    exact (RingHom.congr_fun heB _).trans (MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom_X' _ _ i)

private noncomputable def differenceEnvelope (n : ℕ) :=
  dividedPowerEnvelope s.A
    (MvPolynomial.C.comp (algebraMap s.A (MvPolynomial ι s.A)))
    (polynomialEnvelopeIdeal (RingHom.ker f.toRingHom)
      (liftedDifferenceIndex (ι := ι) n))
    (baseIdeal_le_polynomialEnvelopeIdeal' (A := s.A)
      (algebraMap s.A (MvPolynomial ι s.A)) (RingHom.ker f.toRingHom)
      (basePolynomialIdeal_le_kernel s f) (liftedDifferenceIndex (ι := ι) n))

/-- The comparison `D_{P,γ}(J)⟨x_w : w ∈ W(n)⟩ ≅ D_{Pᵈⁱᶠᶠ,γ}(K(n))` of the divided power
envelope in the difference coordinates with the divided power polynomial algebra over the
envelope of `J`, chosen once from `Crystalline.dividedPowerEnvelopeAddVariables'`. -/
@[no_expose] private noncomputable def addVariablesEquiv (n : ℕ) :=
  Classical.choose (dividedPowerEnvelopeAddVariables' (A := s.A)
    (algebraMap s.A (MvPolynomial ι s.A)) (RingHom.ker f.toRingHom)
    (basePolynomialIdeal_le_kernel s f) (liftedDifferenceIndex (ι := ι) n)
    (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f) (differenceEnvelope s f n))

private theorem addVariablesEquiv_spec (n : ℕ) :
    DividedPowers.IsDPMorphism (differenceEnvelope s f n).object.dividedPowers
        (setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialDividedPowers
          (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).object (liftedDifferenceIndex (ι := ι) n))
        (addVariablesEquiv s f n).toRingHom ∧
      DividedPowers.IsDPMorphism
        (setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialDividedPowers
          (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).object (liftedDifferenceIndex (ι := ι) n))
        (differenceEnvelope s f n).object.dividedPowers
        (addVariablesEquiv s f n).symm.toRingHom ∧
      (∀ b : MvPolynomial ι s.A,
        addVariablesEquiv s f n ((differenceEnvelope s f n).algebraMap.toRingHom
            (MvPolynomial.C b)) =
          algebraMap (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).object
            (setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialAlgebra
              (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).object (liftedDifferenceIndex (ι := ι) n))
            ((polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).algebraMap.toRingHom b)) ∧
      (∀ i : liftedDifferenceIndex (ι := ι) n,
        addVariablesEquiv s f n ((differenceEnvelope s f n).algebraMap.toRingHom
            (MvPolynomial.X i)) =
          dividedPowerPolynomialVariable (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).object i) :=
  Classical.choose_spec (dividedPowerEnvelopeAddVariables' (A := s.A)
    (algebraMap s.A (MvPolynomial ι s.A)) (RingHom.ker f.toRingHom)
    (basePolynomialIdeal_le_kernel s f) (liftedDifferenceIndex (ι := ι) n)
    (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f) (differenceEnvelope s f n))

private theorem tensorBaseIdeal_le_kernel (n : ℕ) :
    s.A.ideal.map (algebraMap s.A (MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1) × ι) s.A)) ≤
      RingHom.ker (tensorPowerPresentation s f n).toRingHom := by
  rw [Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap]
  intro a ha
  have hconst : tensorPowerPresentation s f n
      (algebraMap s.A (MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1) × ι) s.A) a) =
        algebraMap s.A s.C a := by
    simp [tensorPowerPresentation]
  change tensorPowerPresentation s f n
    (algebraMap s.A (MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1) × ι) s.A) a) = 0
  rw [hconst]
  have ha' : algebraMap s.A s.C a ∈ s.A.ideal.map (algebraMap s.A s.C) :=
    Ideal.mem_map_of_mem (algebraMap s.A s.C) ha
  rwa [s.ideal_map_eq_bot] at ha'

private noncomputable def tensorEnvelopeDifferenceEquivData (n : ℕ) :
    {e : (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s
      (tensorPowerPresentation s f n)).object.carrier ≃+*
        (differenceEnvelope s f n).object.carrier //
      (e.toRingHom.comp (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s
        (tensorPowerPresentation s f n)).algebraMap.toRingHom =
        (differenceEnvelope s f n).algebraMap.toRingHom.comp
          (tensorDifferenceCoordinates s n).toRingHom) ∧
        DividedPowers.IsDPMorphism (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s
            (tensorPowerPresentation s f n)).object.dividedPowers
          (differenceEnvelope s f n).object.dividedPowers e.toRingHom ∧
        DividedPowers.IsDPMorphism (differenceEnvelope s f n).object.dividedPowers
          (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s
            (tensorPowerPresentation s f n)).object.dividedPowers e.symm.toRingHom ∧
        e.toRingHom.comp (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s
            (tensorPowerPresentation s f n)).structureMap.toRingHom =
          (differenceEnvelope s f n).structureMap.toRingHom} := by
  let W := liftedDifferenceIndex (ι := ι) n
  let F := tensorDifferenceCoordinates (ι := ι) s n
  let K := polynomialEnvelopeIdeal (RingHom.ker f.toRingHom) W
  let hK := tensorKernel_map_differenceCoordinates s f n
  have hK' : Ideal.map F.toRingHom
      (RingHom.ker (tensorPowerPresentation s f n).toRingHom) = K := hK
  have hcomp : F.symm.toRingHom.comp F.toRingHom = RingHom.id _ :=
    RingHom.ext F.symm_apply_apply
  have hKinv : Ideal.map F.symm.toRingHom K ≤
      RingHom.ker (tensorPowerPresentation s f n).toRingHom := by
    rw [← hK']
    calc
      Ideal.map F.symm.toRingHom (Ideal.map F.toRingHom
          (RingHom.ker (tensorPowerPresentation s f n).toRingHom)) =
          Ideal.map (F.symm.toRingHom.comp F.toRingHom)
            (RingHom.ker (tensorPowerPresentation s f n).toRingHom) := by
              rw [← Ideal.map_map]
      _ ≤ RingHom.ker (tensorPowerPresentation s f n).toRingHom := by
        rw [hcomp]
        simp
  have hbase : F.toRingHom.comp
      (algebraMap s.A (MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1) × ι) s.A)) =
        (MvPolynomial.C.comp (algebraMap s.A (MvPolynomial ι s.A))) := by
    ext a
    simp [F, tensorDifferenceCoordinates, differenceIndexEquiv,
      differenceShiftEquiv, differenceShiftHom]
  let hEquiv := dividedPowerEnvelopeEquivOfPresentationEquiv
    (algebraMap s.A (MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1) × ι) s.A))
    (RingHom.ker (tensorPowerPresentation s f n).toRingHom)
    (tensorBaseIdeal_le_kernel s f n)
    (MvPolynomial.C.comp (algebraMap s.A (MvPolynomial ι s.A))) K
    (baseIdeal_le_polynomialEnvelopeIdeal' (A := s.A)
      (algebraMap s.A (MvPolynomial ι s.A)) (RingHom.ker f.toRingHom)
      (basePolynomialIdeal_le_kernel s f) W)
    F hbase hK'.le hKinv
    (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s
      (tensorPowerPresentation s f n)) (differenceEnvelope s f n)
  let e := Classical.choose hEquiv
  exact ⟨e, Classical.choose_spec hEquiv⟩

private theorem tensorEnvelopeDifferenceEquivData_algebraMap (n : ℕ)
    (y : MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1) × ι) s.A) :
    (tensorEnvelopeDifferenceEquivData s f n).1
        ((polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s
          (tensorPowerPresentation s f n)).algebraMap.toRingHom y) =
      (differenceEnvelope s f n).algebraMap.toRingHom (tensorDifferenceCoordinates s n y) :=
  RingHom.congr_fun (tensorEnvelopeDifferenceEquivData s f n).property.1 y

private noncomputable def tensorEnvelopeDifferenceEquiv (n : ℕ) :
    (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s
      (tensorPowerPresentation s f n)).object.carrier ≃+*
      (differenceEnvelope s f n).object.carrier :=
  (tensorEnvelopeDifferenceEquivData s f n).1

private noncomputable def tensorEnvelopeDividedPowerEquiv (n : ℕ) :
    (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s
      (tensorPowerPresentation s f n)).object.carrier ≃+*
      setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialAlgebra
        (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).object (ι × Fin n) :=
  (tensorEnvelopeDifferenceEquiv s f n).trans
    ((addVariablesEquiv s f n).trans
      (dividedPowerPolynomialIndexEquiv (ι := ι) n (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).object
        |>.toRingEquiv))

private noncomputable def completedTensorEnvelopeDividedPowerEquiv (n : ℕ) :
    pAdicCompletedTensorPowerEnvelope s f hf n ≃+*
      AdicCompletion
        (pIdeal
          (setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialAlgebra
            (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).object (ι × Fin n)) s.p)
        (setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialAlgebra
          (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).object (ι × Fin n)) :=
  pAdicCompletionEquiv (tensorEnvelopeDividedPowerEquiv s f n) s.p

private theorem tensorEnvelopeDividedPowerEquiv_coprojection (n : ℕ)
    (x : MvPolynomial ι s.A) :
    tensorEnvelopeDividedPowerEquiv s f n
        ((polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s
          (tensorPowerPresentation s f n)).algebraMap.toRingHom
          (mvPolynomialCoprojection s.A (0 : Fin (n + 1)) x)) =
      algebraMap
        (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).object
        (setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialAlgebra
          (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).object (ι × Fin n))
        ((polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).algebraMap.toRingHom x) := by
  change dividedPowerPolynomialIndexEquiv (ι := ι) n (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).object
    (addVariablesEquiv s f n ((tensorEnvelopeDifferenceEquivData s f n).1 _)) = _
  rw [tensorEnvelopeDifferenceEquivData_algebraMap, tensorDifferenceCoordinates_coprojection,
    (addVariablesEquiv_spec s f n).2.2.1]
  exact AlgEquiv.commutes _ _

private theorem tensorEnvelopeDividedPowerEquiv_coprojectionDifference (n : ℕ) (q : ι × Fin n) :
    tensorEnvelopeDividedPowerEquiv s f n
        ((polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s
          (tensorPowerPresentation s f n)).algebraMap.toRingHom (coprojectionDifference s n q)) =
      dividedPowerPolynomialVariable
        (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).object q := by
  change dividedPowerPolynomialIndexEquiv (ι := ι) n (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).object
    (addVariablesEquiv s f n ((tensorEnvelopeDifferenceEquivData s f n).1 _)) = _
  rw [tensorEnvelopeDifferenceEquivData_algebraMap,
    tensorDifferenceCoordinates_coprojectionDifference, (addVariablesEquiv_spec s f n).2.2.2]
  change DividedPowerAlgebra.map _
    (Finsupp.lmapDomain _ _ ULift.down)
    (dividedPowerPolynomialVariable _ (ULift.up q)) = _
  simp [dividedPowerPolynomialVariable, DividedPowerAlgebra.map_apply_dp]

private theorem pAdicCompletionEquiv_algebraMap {R S : Type*}
    [CommRing R] [CommRing S] (e : R ≃+* S) (p : ℕ) (x : R) :
    pAdicCompletionEquiv e p
        (algebraMap R (AdicCompletion (Ideal.span {(p : R)}) R) x) =
      algebraMap S (AdicCompletion (Ideal.span {(p : S)}) S) (e x) := by
  apply AdicCompletion.ext_evalₐ
  intro n
  change AdicCompletion.evalₐ (Ideal.span {(p : S)}) n
      (adicCompletionMap e.toRingHom (Ideal.span {(p : R)})
        (Ideal.span {(p : S)}) (pIdeal_map_le e.toRingHom p) (algebraMap R _ x)) = _
  rw [show algebraMap R (AdicCompletion (Ideal.span {(p : R)}) R) x =
      AdicCompletion.of (Ideal.span {(p : R)}) R x from rfl,
    adicCompletionMap_evalₐ, AdicCompletion.evalₐ_of]
  simp

private noncomputable def pQuotMap {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    (g : R →+* S) (p n : ℕ) : R ⧸ pIdeal R p ^ n →+* S ⧸ pIdeal S p ^ n :=
  Ideal.quotientMap _ g (Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mp (by
    rw [Ideal.map_pow]; exact Ideal.pow_right_mono (pIdeal_map_le g p) n))

private theorem pQuotMap_mk {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    (g : R →+* S) (p n : ℕ) (x : R) :
    pQuotMap g p n (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ x) = Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (g x) := rfl

private theorem basis_mem_pIdeal_pow {R B κ : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing B]
    [Algebra R B] (b : Module.Basis κ R B) (p n : ℕ) (x : B) :
    x ∈ pIdeal B p ^ n ↔ ∀ i, b.repr x i ∈ pIdeal R p ^ n := by
  classical
  simp only [pIdeal, Ideal.span_singleton_pow, Ideal.mem_span_singleton]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨y, rfl⟩ i
    refine ⟨b.repr y i, ?_⟩
    have h : (p : B) ^ n * y = (p : R) ^ n • y := by simp [Algebra.smul_def]
    rw [h, map_smul]
    rfl
  · intro h
    rw [← b.linearCombination_repr x, Finsupp.linearCombination_apply, Finsupp.sum]
    apply Finset.dvd_sum
    intro i hi
    obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := h i
    refine ⟨r • b i, ?_⟩
    rw [hr, mul_smul]
    simp [Algebra.smul_def]

private theorem basis_map_repr {R S B C κ : Type*}
    [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [CommRing B] [CommRing C]
    [Algebra R B] [Algebra S C] (b : Module.Basis κ R B) (c : Module.Basis κ S C)
    (g : R →+* S) (F : B →+* C)
    (hcoeff : ∀ r, F (algebraMap R B r) = algebraMap S C (g r))
    (hb : ∀ i, F (b i) = c i) (x : B) (i : κ) :
    c.repr (F x) i = g (b.repr x i) := by
  classical
  have hsum : F x = (b.repr x).sum (fun j r => g r • c j) := by
    conv_lhs => rw [← b.linearCombination_repr x, Finsupp.linearCombination_apply, Finsupp.sum]
    simp [Finsupp.sum, map_sum, Algebra.smul_def, hcoeff, hb]
  rw [hsum]
  have hz : b.repr x i = 0 → 0 = g (b.repr x i) := by
    intro h
    rw [h, map_zero]
  simpa [Finsupp.sum, map_sum, map_smul, Module.Basis.repr_self,
    Finsupp.smul_single, Finsupp.single_apply, Finset.sum_ite_eq', Finsupp.mem_support_iff]
    using hz

private theorem basis_pQuotMap_bijective {R S B C κ : Type*}
    [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [CommRing B] [CommRing C]
    [Algebra R B] [Algebra S C] (b : Module.Basis κ R B) (c : Module.Basis κ S C)
    (g : R →+* S) (F : B →+* C)
    (hcoeff : ∀ r, F (algebraMap R B r) = algebraMap S C (g r))
    (hb : ∀ i, F (b i) = c i) (p n : ℕ)
    (hg : Function.Bijective (pQuotMap g p n)) :
    Function.Bijective (pQuotMap F p n) := by
  classical
  have hmem : ∀ x : B, F x ∈ pIdeal C p ^ n → x ∈ pIdeal B p ^ n := by
    intro x hx
    rw [basis_mem_pIdeal_pow b]
    intro i
    have hi := (basis_mem_pIdeal_pow c p n (F x)).mp hx i
    rw [basis_map_repr b c g F hcoeff hb] at hi
    apply Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mp
    apply hg.1
    simpa [pQuotMap_mk] using Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mpr hi
  constructor
  · apply (RingHom.injective_iff_ker_eq_bot _).mpr
    apply le_antisymm _ bot_le
    intro x hx
    obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective x
    have hy : F y ∈ pIdeal C p ^ n := Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mp hx
    exact Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mpr (hmem y hy)
  · intro y
    obtain ⟨z, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective y
    have hlift : ∀ i, ∃ r : R,
        Ideal.Quotient.mk (pIdeal S p ^ n) (g r) =
          Ideal.Quotient.mk (pIdeal S p ^ n) (c.repr z i) := by
      intro i
      obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := hg.2 (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (c.repr z i))
      obtain ⟨r, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective r
      exact ⟨r, hr⟩
    choose r hr using hlift
    let x := ∑ i ∈ (c.repr z).support, r i • b i
    refine ⟨Ideal.Quotient.mk _ x, ?_⟩
    rw [pQuotMap_mk, Ideal.Quotient.eq]
    have hz : F x - z = ∑ i ∈ (c.repr z).support,
        (g (r i) - c.repr z i) • c i := by
      conv_lhs =>
        rhs
        rw [← c.linearCombination_repr z, Finsupp.linearCombination_apply, Finsupp.sum]
      simp [x, map_sum, Algebra.smul_def, hcoeff, hb,
        Finset.sum_sub_distrib, sub_mul]
    rw [hz]
    apply Ideal.sum_mem
    intro i hi
    have hri : g (r i) - c.repr z i ∈ pIdeal S p ^ n :=
      Ideal.Quotient.eq.mp (hr i)
    have hm := Ideal.mem_map_of_mem (algebraMap S C) hri
    have hle : (pIdeal S p ^ n).map (algebraMap S C) ≤ pIdeal C p ^ n := by
      rw [Ideal.map_pow]
      exact Ideal.pow_right_mono (pIdeal_map_le _ p) n
    simpa only [Algebra.smul_def] using Ideal.mul_mem_right (c i) _ (hle hm)

private theorem completion_ker_eval {R : Type*} [CommRing R] (p n : ℕ) :
    RingHom.ker (AdicCompletion.evalₐ (pIdeal R p) n).toRingHom =
      pIdeal (AdicCompletion (pIdeal R p) R) p ^ n := by
  have heq : pIdeal (AdicCompletion (pIdeal R p) R) p ^ n =
      (pIdeal R p ^ n).map (algebraMap R (AdicCompletion (pIdeal R p) R)) := by
    simp [pIdeal, Ideal.map_pow, Ideal.map_span]
  rw [heq]
  ext x
  rw [RingHom.mem_ker]
  change AdicCompletion.evalₐ (pIdeal R p) n x = 0 ↔ _
  rw [← Submodule.restrictScalars_mem R, ← Ideal.smul_top_eq_map,
    AdicCompletion.pow_smul_top_eq_ker_eval (Submodule.fg_span_singleton _)]
  have h : pIdeal R p ^ n * ⊤ = pIdeal R p ^ n := by simp
  have hinj : Function.Injective (Ideal.Quotient.factor (le_of_eq h)) := by
    simpa [RingHom.injective_iff_ker_eq_bot, Ideal.Quotient.factor_ker] using
      Ideal.map_mk_eq_bot_of_le (le_of_eq h.symm)
  simpa [← AdicCompletion.factor_eval_eq_evalₐ] using map_eq_zero_iff _ hinj

private theorem completion_pQuotMap_bijective (R : Type*) [CommRing R] (p n : ℕ) :
    Function.Bijective (pQuotMap (algebraMap R (AdicCompletion (pIdeal R p) R)) p n) := by
  let I := pIdeal R p
  let S := AdicCompletion I R
  let g := algebraMap R S
  let E := AdicCompletion.evalₐ I n
  have hker : ∀ x : S, E x = 0 ↔ x ∈ pIdeal S p ^ n := by
    intro x
    change x ∈ RingHom.ker E.toRingHom ↔ _
    rw [completion_ker_eval]
  constructor
  · apply (RingHom.injective_iff_ker_eq_bot _).mpr
    apply le_antisymm _ bot_le
    intro x hx
    obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective x
    have ha : g a ∈ pIdeal S p ^ n := Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mp hx
    have := (hker (g a)).mpr ha
    change AdicCompletion.evalₐ I n (AdicCompletion.of I R a) = 0 at this
    simpa only [AdicCompletion.evalₐ_of, Ideal.mem_bot] using this
  · intro y
    obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective y
    obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective (E x)
    refine ⟨Ideal.Quotient.mk _ a, ?_⟩
    rw [pQuotMap_mk, Ideal.Quotient.eq]
    apply (hker _).mp
    change E (g a - x) = 0
    rw [map_sub]
    change AdicCompletion.evalₐ I n (AdicCompletion.of I R a) - E x = 0
    rw [AdicCompletion.evalₐ_of, ha, sub_self]

private noncomputable def dpCoefficients {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    [Algebra R S] (W : Type*) :
    DividedPowerAlgebra R (W →₀ R) →ₐ[R] DividedPowerAlgebra S (W →₀ S) :=
  DividedPowerAlgebra.map S (Finsupp.mapRange.linearMap (Algebra.linearMap R S))

private theorem dpCoefficients_basis {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    [Algebra R S] (W : Type*) (i : W →₀ ℕ) :
    dpCoefficients (R := R) (S := S) W (dividedPowerPolynomialMonomialBasis R W i) =
      dividedPowerPolynomialMonomialBasis S W i := by
  classical
  simp only [dividedPowerPolynomialMonomialBasis_apply, dividedPowerPolynomialMonomial,
    Finsupp.prod, map_prod]
  apply Finset.prod_congr rfl
  intro j hj
  simp [dpCoefficients, DividedPowerAlgebra.map_apply_dp]

private theorem dpCoefficients_dividedPowerPolynomialVariable {R S : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] (W : Type*) (q : W) :
    dpCoefficients (R := R) (S := S) W (dividedPowerPolynomialVariable R q) =
      dividedPowerPolynomialVariable S q := by
  simp [dpCoefficients, dividedPowerPolynomialVariable, DividedPowerAlgebra.map_apply_dp]

private theorem dpCoefficients_pQuotMap_bijective {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    [Algebra R S] (W : Type*) (p n : ℕ)
    (h : Function.Bijective (pQuotMap (algebraMap R S) p n)) :
    Function.Bijective (pQuotMap (dpCoefficients (R := R) (S := S) W).toRingHom p n) :=
  basis_pQuotMap_bijective (dividedPowerPolynomialMonomialBasis R W)
    (dividedPowerPolynomialMonomialBasis S W) (algebraMap R S) _
    (fun r => (dpCoefficients W).commutes r) (dpCoefficients_basis W) p n h

private theorem pQuotMap_factor {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    (g : R →+* S) (p : ℕ) {m n : ℕ} (h : m ≤ n) (x : R ⧸ pIdeal R p ^ n) :
    pQuotMap g p m (Ideal.Quotient.factorPow (pIdeal R p) h x) =
      Ideal.Quotient.factorPow (pIdeal S p) h (pQuotMap g p n x) := by
  obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective x
  rfl

private noncomputable abbrev completionMap {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    (g : R →+* S) (p : ℕ) :
    AdicCompletion (pIdeal R p) R →+* AdicCompletion (pIdeal S p) S :=
  adicCompletionMap g (pIdeal R p) (pIdeal S p) (pIdeal_map_le g p)

private theorem completionMap_eval {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    (g : R →+* S) (p n : ℕ) (x : AdicCompletion (pIdeal R p) R) :
    AdicCompletion.evalₐ (pIdeal S p) n (completionMap g p x) =
      pQuotMap g p n (AdicCompletion.evalₐ (pIdeal R p) n x) :=
  adicCompletionMap_evalₐ g _ _ _ n x

private theorem completionMap_of {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    (g : R →+* S) (p : ℕ) (x : R) :
    completionMap g p (algebraMap R _ x) = algebraMap S _ (g x) := by
  apply AdicCompletion.ext_evalₐ
  intro n
  rw [completionMap_eval]
  change pQuotMap g p n (AdicCompletion.evalₐ (pIdeal R p) n
    (AdicCompletion.of (pIdeal R p) R x)) =
      AdicCompletion.evalₐ (pIdeal S p) n (AdicCompletion.of (pIdeal S p) S (g x))
  rw [AdicCompletion.evalₐ_of, AdicCompletion.evalₐ_of]
  rfl

private noncomputable def completionEquivOfQuotientBijective {R S : Type*}
    [CommRing R] [CommRing S] (g : R →+* S) (p : ℕ)
    (hg : ∀ n, Function.Bijective (pQuotMap g p n)) :
    AdicCompletion (pIdeal R p) R ≃+* AdicCompletion (pIdeal S p) S := by
  let e (n : ℕ) := RingEquiv.ofBijective (pQuotMap g p n) (hg n)
  let inv := AdicCompletion.liftRingHom (pIdeal R p)
    (fun n => (e n).symm.toRingHom.comp (AdicCompletion.evalₐ (pIdeal S p) n).toRingHom)
    (by
      intro m n h
      ext x
      apply (e m).injective
      change pQuotMap g p m
          (Ideal.Quotient.factorPow (pIdeal R p) h
            ((e n).symm (AdicCompletion.evalₐ (pIdeal S p) n x))) = _
      rw [pQuotMap_factor]
      change Ideal.Quotient.factorPow (pIdeal S p) h
        ((e n) ((e n).symm (AdicCompletion.evalₐ (pIdeal S p) n x))) =
          (e m) ((e m).symm (AdicCompletion.evalₐ (pIdeal S p) m x))
      simp only [RingEquiv.apply_symm_apply,
        AdicCompletion.factorPow_evalₐ])
  apply RingEquiv.ofRingHom (completionMap g p) inv
  · apply RingHom.ext
    intro x
    apply AdicCompletion.ext_evalₐ
    intro n
    rw [RingHom.comp_apply, completionMap_eval]
    change pQuotMap g p n (AdicCompletion.evalₐ (pIdeal R p) n (inv x)) = _
    rw [AdicCompletion.evalₐ_liftRingHom]
    exact (e n).apply_symm_apply _
  · apply RingHom.ext
    intro x
    apply AdicCompletion.ext_evalₐ
    intro n
    change AdicCompletion.evalₐ (pIdeal R p) n (inv (completionMap g p x)) = _
    rw [AdicCompletion.evalₐ_liftRingHom]
    change (e n).symm (AdicCompletion.evalₐ (pIdeal S p) n (completionMap g p x)) = _
    rw [completionMap_eval]
    exact (e n).symm_apply_apply _

private noncomputable def completedDPCoefficientsEquiv {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    [Algebra R S] (W : Type*) (p : ℕ)
    (h : ∀ n, Function.Bijective (pQuotMap (algebraMap R S) p n)) :
    AdicCompletion (pIdeal (DividedPowerAlgebra R (W →₀ R)) p)
        (DividedPowerAlgebra R (W →₀ R)) ≃+*
      AdicCompletion (pIdeal (DividedPowerAlgebra S (W →₀ S)) p)
        (DividedPowerAlgebra S (W →₀ S)) :=
  completionEquivOfQuotientBijective (dpCoefficients W).toRingHom p
    fun n => dpCoefficients_pQuotMap_bijective W p n (h n)

private theorem completedDPCoefficientsEquiv_of {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    [Algebra R S] (W : Type*) (p : ℕ)
    (h : ∀ n, Function.Bijective (pQuotMap (algebraMap R S) p n))
    (x : DividedPowerAlgebra R (W →₀ R)) :
    completedDPCoefficientsEquiv W p h (algebraMap _ _ x) =
      algebraMap _ _ (dpCoefficients (S := S) W x) :=
  completionMap_of _ _ _

/-! ### The completed divided power polynomial algebra `lim_e D⟨ξ_i(j)⟩/p^e D⟨ξ_i(j)⟩` -/

/-- The divided power polynomial algebra `D⟨ξ_i(j)⟩` over `D`, with one divided power
variable `ξ_i(j)` for every `i` and every `j = 1, …, n`. -/
public noncomputable abbrev dividedPowerPolynomialOverEnvelope (n : ℕ) : Type (max u w) :=
  setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialAlgebra
    (pAdicCompletedDividedPowerEnvelope s f hf) (ι × Fin n)

/-- The right hand side `lim_e D⟨ξ_i(j)⟩/p^e D⟨ξ_i(j)⟩` of the displayed isomorphism: the
`p`-adic completion of the divided power polynomial algebra `D⟨ξ_i(j)⟩`. -/
public noncomputable abbrev pAdicCompletedDividedPowerPolynomialOverEnvelope (n : ℕ) :
    Type (max u w) :=
  AdicCompletion
    (Ideal.span {(s.p : dividedPowerPolynomialOverEnvelope s f hf n)})
    (dividedPowerPolynomialOverEnvelope s f hf n)

/-- The structure map `D → lim_e D⟨ξ_i(j)⟩/p^e D⟨ξ_i(j)⟩` making the right hand side of the
displayed isomorphism an algebra over `D`. -/
public noncomputable def toPAdicCompletedDividedPowerPolynomial (n : ℕ) :
    pAdicCompletedDividedPowerEnvelope s f hf →+*
      pAdicCompletedDividedPowerPolynomialOverEnvelope s f hf n :=
  (algebraMap (dividedPowerPolynomialOverEnvelope s f hf n)
      (pAdicCompletedDividedPowerPolynomialOverEnvelope s f hf n)).comp
    (algebraMap (pAdicCompletedDividedPowerEnvelope s f hf)
      (dividedPowerPolynomialOverEnvelope s f hf n))

/-- The divided power variable `ξ_i(j)` of `D⟨ξ_i(j)⟩`, viewed in the `p`-adic
completion `lim_e D⟨ξ_i(j)⟩/p^e D⟨ξ_i(j)⟩`. -/
public noncomputable def coprojectionDifferenceVariable (n : ℕ) (q : ι × Fin n) :
    pAdicCompletedDividedPowerPolynomialOverEnvelope s f hf n :=
  algebraMap (dividedPowerPolynomialOverEnvelope s f hf n)
      (pAdicCompletedDividedPowerPolynomialOverEnvelope s f hf n)
    (dividedPowerPolynomialVariable
      (pAdicCompletedDividedPowerEnvelope s f hf) q)

/-! ### The lemma -/

/-- The composite `P → D → lim_e D⟨ξ_i(j)⟩/p^e D⟨ξ_i(j)⟩` is the coefficient map of the
divided power polynomial algebra, composed with the map to the envelope and the completion. -/
private theorem toPAdicCompletedDividedPowerPolynomial_apply (n : ℕ) (x : MvPolynomial ι s.A) :
    toPAdicCompletedDividedPowerPolynomial s f hf n
        (toPAdicCompletedDividedPowerEnvelope s f hf x) =
      algebraMap (dividedPowerPolynomialOverEnvelope s f hf n)
          (pAdicCompletedDividedPowerPolynomialOverEnvelope s f hf n)
        (algebraMap (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).object
          (dividedPowerPolynomialOverEnvelope s f hf n)
          ((polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).algebraMap.toRingHom x)) :=
  congrArg
    (algebraMap (dividedPowerPolynomialOverEnvelope s f hf n)
      (pAdicCompletedDividedPowerPolynomialOverEnvelope s f hf n))
    (IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).object
        (pAdicCompletedDividedPowerEnvelope s f hf)
        (dividedPowerPolynomialOverEnvelope s f hf n)
        ((polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).algebraMap.toRingHom x)).symm

/-- The divided power polynomial algebra `D_{P, γ}(J)⟨ξ_i(j)⟩` on the `ξ_i(j)` over the
uncompleted divided power envelope. -/
private abbrev uncompletedDividedPowerPolynomial (n : ℕ) : Type (max u w) :=
  setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialAlgebra (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).object (ι × Fin n)

/-- Reducing coefficients along `D_{P, γ}(J) → D` is bijective modulo every power of `p`. -/
private theorem envelopeCompletion_pQuotMap_bijective (n : ℕ) :
    Function.Bijective (pQuotMap (algebraMap (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).object
      (pAdicCompletedDividedPowerEnvelope s f hf)) s.p n) :=
  completion_pQuotMap_bijective _ s.p n

/-- The comparison `lim_e D_{P, γ}(J)⟨ξ_i(j)⟩/p^e = lim_e D⟨ξ_i(j)⟩/p^e` of the two completed
divided power polynomial algebras, obtained from the freeness on divided power monomials. -/
private noncomputable def envelopeCoefficientsEquiv (n : ℕ) :
    AdicCompletion (pIdeal (uncompletedDividedPowerPolynomial s f n) s.p)
        (uncompletedDividedPowerPolynomial s f n) ≃+*
      pAdicCompletedDividedPowerPolynomialOverEnvelope s f hf n :=
  completedDPCoefficientsEquiv (R := (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).object)
    (S := pAdicCompletedDividedPowerEnvelope s f hf) (ι × Fin n) s.p
    (envelopeCompletion_pQuotMap_bijective s f hf)

private theorem envelopeCoefficientsEquiv_of (n : ℕ)
    (x : uncompletedDividedPowerPolynomial s f n) :
    envelopeCoefficientsEquiv s f hf n
        (algebraMap (uncompletedDividedPowerPolynomial s f n)
          (AdicCompletion (pIdeal (uncompletedDividedPowerPolynomial s f n) s.p)
            (uncompletedDividedPowerPolynomial s f n)) x) =
      algebraMap (dividedPowerPolynomialOverEnvelope s f hf n)
        (pAdicCompletedDividedPowerPolynomialOverEnvelope s f hf n)
        (dpCoefficients (S := pAdicCompletedDividedPowerEnvelope s f hf) (ι × Fin n) x) :=
  completedDPCoefficientsEquiv_of (ι × Fin n) s.p _ x

/-- The isomorphism `D(n) = lim_e D⟨ξ_i(j)⟩/p^e D⟨ξ_i(j)⟩`: the identification of the divided
power envelope of `J(n)` with the divided power polynomial algebra on the `ξ_i(j)` over the
divided power envelope of `J`, followed by the comparison of the two completions. -/
private noncomputable def tensorPowerStructureEquiv (n : ℕ) :
    pAdicCompletedTensorPowerEnvelope s f hf n ≃+*
      pAdicCompletedDividedPowerPolynomialOverEnvelope s f hf n :=
  (completedTensorEnvelopeDividedPowerEquiv s f hf n).trans (envelopeCoefficientsEquiv s f hf n)

/-- The map `P → D` is the map to the divided power envelope followed by the map to its
`p`-adic completion. -/
private theorem toPAdicCompletedDividedPowerEnvelope_apply {κ : Type*}
    (g : MvPolynomial κ s.A →ₐ[s.A] s.C) (hg : Function.Surjective g)
    (y : MvPolynomial κ s.A) :
    toPAdicCompletedDividedPowerEnvelope s g hg y =
      algebraMap (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s g).object
        (pAdicCompletedDividedPowerEnvelope s g hg)
        ((polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s g).algebraMap.toRingHom y) :=
  rfl

private theorem tensorPowerStructureEquiv_apply (n : ℕ)
    (z : pAdicCompletedTensorPowerEnvelope s f hf n) :
    tensorPowerStructureEquiv s f hf n z =
      envelopeCoefficientsEquiv s f hf n
        (completedTensorEnvelopeDividedPowerEquiv s f hf n z) :=
  RingEquiv.trans_apply _ _ z

/-- On the image of the tensor power, the comparison of the completions is the comparison of
the uncompleted envelopes. -/
private theorem completedTensorEnvelopeDividedPowerEquiv_toPAdic (n : ℕ)
    (y : MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1) × ι) s.A) :
    completedTensorEnvelopeDividedPowerEquiv s f hf n
        (toPAdicCompletedDividedPowerEnvelope s (tensorPowerPresentation s f n)
          (tensorPowerPresentation_surjective s f hf n) y) =
      algebraMap (uncompletedDividedPowerPolynomial s f n)
          (AdicCompletion (pIdeal (uncompletedDividedPowerPolynomial s f n) s.p)
            (uncompletedDividedPowerPolynomial s f n))
        (tensorEnvelopeDividedPowerEquiv s f n
          ((polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s (tensorPowerPresentation s f n)).algebraMap.toRingHom
            y)) :=
  pAdicCompletionEquiv_algebraMap (tensorEnvelopeDividedPowerEquiv s f n) s.p _

/-- The comparison carries the image of an element of the tensor power to the image of its
image under the identification of the uncompleted envelopes. -/
private theorem tensorPowerStructureEquiv_toPAdic (n : ℕ)
    (y : MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1) × ι) s.A) :
    tensorPowerStructureEquiv s f hf n
        (toPAdicCompletedDividedPowerEnvelope s (tensorPowerPresentation s f n)
          (tensorPowerPresentation_surjective s f hf n) y) =
      envelopeCoefficientsEquiv s f hf n
        (algebraMap (uncompletedDividedPowerPolynomial s f n)
            (AdicCompletion (pIdeal (uncompletedDividedPowerPolynomial s f n) s.p)
              (uncompletedDividedPowerPolynomial s f n))
          (tensorEnvelopeDividedPowerEquiv s f n
            ((polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s (tensorPowerPresentation s f n)).algebraMap.toRingHom
              y))) :=
  (tensorPowerStructureEquiv_apply s f hf n _).trans
    (congrArg
      (fun z : pAdicCompletedTensorPowerEnvelope s f hf n =>
        envelopeCoefficientsEquiv s f hf n (completedTensorEnvelopeDividedPowerEquiv s f hf n z))
      (toPAdicCompletedDividedPowerEnvelope_apply s (tensorPowerPresentation s f n)
          (tensorPowerPresentation_surjective s f hf n) y) |>.trans
      (congrArg (fun z => envelopeCoefficientsEquiv s f hf n z)
        (completedTensorEnvelopeDividedPowerEquiv_toPAdic s f hf n y)))

private theorem tensorPowerStructureEquiv_coprojection (n : ℕ) (x : MvPolynomial ι s.A) :
    tensorPowerStructureEquiv s f hf n
        (toPAdicCompletedDividedPowerEnvelope s (tensorPowerPresentation s f n)
          (tensorPowerPresentation_surjective s f hf n)
          (mvPolynomialCoprojection s.A (0 : Fin (n + 1)) x)) =
      toPAdicCompletedDividedPowerPolynomial s f hf n
        (toPAdicCompletedDividedPowerEnvelope s f hf x) :=
  (tensorPowerStructureEquiv_toPAdic s f hf n _).trans
    ((congrArg
          (fun z : uncompletedDividedPowerPolynomial s f n =>
            envelopeCoefficientsEquiv s f hf n (algebraMap _ _ z))
          (tensorEnvelopeDividedPowerEquiv_coprojection s f n x)).trans
      ((envelopeCoefficientsEquiv_of s f hf n _).trans
        ((congrArg
              (fun z : dividedPowerPolynomialOverEnvelope s f hf n =>
                algebraMap (dividedPowerPolynomialOverEnvelope s f hf n)
                  (pAdicCompletedDividedPowerPolynomialOverEnvelope s f hf n) z)
              ((dpCoefficients (S := pAdicCompletedDividedPowerEnvelope s f hf)
                (ι × Fin n)).commutes
                ((polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).algebraMap.toRingHom x))).trans
          (toPAdicCompletedDividedPowerPolynomial_apply s f hf n x).symm)))

private theorem tensorPowerStructureEquiv_coprojectionDifference (n : ℕ) (q : ι × Fin n) :
    tensorPowerStructureEquiv s f hf n
        (toPAdicCompletedDividedPowerEnvelope s (tensorPowerPresentation s f n)
          (tensorPowerPresentation_surjective s f hf n) (coprojectionDifference s n q)) =
      coprojectionDifferenceVariable s f hf n q :=
  (tensorPowerStructureEquiv_toPAdic s f hf n _).trans
    ((congrArg
          (fun z : uncompletedDividedPowerPolynomial s f n =>
            envelopeCoefficientsEquiv s f hf n (algebraMap _ _ z))
          (tensorEnvelopeDividedPowerEquiv_coprojectionDifference s f n q)).trans
      ((envelopeCoefficientsEquiv_of s f hf n _).trans
        (congrArg
          (fun z : dividedPowerPolynomialOverEnvelope s f hf n =>
            algebraMap (dividedPowerPolynomialOverEnvelope s f hf n)
              (pAdicCompletedDividedPowerPolynomialOverEnvelope s f hf n) z)
          (dpCoefficients_dividedPowerPolynomialVariable (ι × Fin n) q))))

/-- **Stacks Project, Lemma 60.17.5, Tag 07L2.** Let `D` and `D(n)` be as in (07J8) and
(07JF).  The coprojection `P → P ⊗_A … ⊗_A P`, `h ↦ h ⊗ 1 ⊗ … ⊗ 1` induces an isomorphism

`D(n) = lim_e D⟨ξ_i(j)⟩/p^e D⟨ξ_i(j)⟩`

of algebras over `D`, with `ξ_i(j) = x_i ⊗ 1 ⊗ … ⊗ 1 - 1 ⊗ … ⊗ 1 ⊗ x_i ⊗ 1 ⊗ … ⊗ 1` for
`j = 1, …, n`, where the second `x_i` is placed in the `(j + 1)`-st slot.

The map `φ` induced by the coprojection is the algebra structure of `D(n)` over `D`: it
agrees with the coprojection on the image of `P`.  The isomorphism `e` is an isomorphism
over `φ`, and it carries the image of `ξ_i(j)` in `D(n)` to the divided power variable
`ξ_i(j)`. -/
@[stacks 07L2]
public theorem exists_ringEquiv_pAdicCompletedDividedPowerPolynomial (n : ℕ) :
    ∃ (φ : pAdicCompletedDividedPowerEnvelope s f hf →+*
        pAdicCompletedTensorPowerEnvelope s f hf n)
      (e : pAdicCompletedTensorPowerEnvelope s f hf n ≃+*
        pAdicCompletedDividedPowerPolynomialOverEnvelope s f hf n),
      (∀ x : MvPolynomial ι s.A,
          φ (toPAdicCompletedDividedPowerEnvelope s f hf x) =
            toPAdicCompletedDividedPowerEnvelope s (tensorPowerPresentation s f n)
              (tensorPowerPresentation_surjective s f hf n)
              (mvPolynomialCoprojection s.A (0 : Fin (n + 1)) x)) ∧
      (∀ y : pAdicCompletedDividedPowerEnvelope s f hf,
          e (φ y) = toPAdicCompletedDividedPowerPolynomial s f hf n y) ∧
      (∀ q : ι × Fin n,
          e (toPAdicCompletedDividedPowerEnvelope s (tensorPowerPresentation s f n)
            (tensorPowerPresentation_surjective s f hf n) (coprojectionDifference s n q)) =
            coprojectionDifferenceVariable s f hf n q) := by
  refine ⟨(tensorPowerStructureEquiv s f hf n).symm.toRingHom.comp
      (toPAdicCompletedDividedPowerPolynomial s f hf n),
    tensorPowerStructureEquiv s f hf n, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · intro x
    apply (tensorPowerStructureEquiv s f hf n).injective
    rw [tensorPowerStructureEquiv_coprojection]
    exact (tensorPowerStructureEquiv s f hf n).apply_symm_apply _
  · intro y
    exact (tensorPowerStructureEquiv s f hf n).apply_symm_apply _
  · intro q
    exact tensorPowerStructureEquiv_coprojectionDifference s f hf n q


/-! ### The uncompleted identification as an isomorphism of divided power rings

The lemma above identifies `D(n)` with `lim_e D⟨ξ_i(j)⟩/p^e` as a *ring* over `D`.  What a
consumer needs in order to carry the identification through the divided power differentials
`Ω^*` is more: that the identification is a morphism of **divided power** rings over `A`, in
both directions.  Nothing of that is visible in a bare `RingEquiv`, and the divided power data
is destroyed by the completion step — `Crystalline.envelopeCoefficientsEquiv` compares the two
completions through freeness on divided power monomials, not through a divided power morphism of
the uncompleted rings.

So the divided power statement is made here one level down, *before* completing: the divided
power envelope `D_{P ⊗ ⋯ ⊗ P, γ}(J(n))` of `J(n)` is isomorphic, as a divided power ring over
`A`, to the divided power polynomial algebra `D_{P,γ}(J)⟨ξ_i(j)⟩` on the `ξ_i(j)` over the
divided power envelope of `J`.  That is the form in which the identification reaches the forms:
`Crystalline.completedMapDifferentialForms` completes a comparison of forms along a divided
power morphism, so the comparison it needs is exactly this one.
-/

/-- **The divided power envelope of `J(n)` is the divided power polynomial algebra on the
`ξ_i(j)` over the divided power envelope of `J`.**

This is the uncompleted form of [Stacks, Lemma 60.17.5, Tag 07L2]: the isomorphism whose
`p`-adic completion is the displayed isomorphism
`D(n) = lim_e D⟨ξ_i(j)⟩/p^e D⟨ξ_i(j)⟩` of that lemma, the completion of the right hand side
being taken along `(p)` of the uncompleted divided power polynomial algebra over the
*uncompleted* envelope.  Unlike the completed statement it is an isomorphism of divided power
rings over `A`, by `Crystalline.tensorEnvelopeDPEquiv_isDPMorphism`,
`Crystalline.tensorEnvelopeDPEquiv_symm_isDPMorphism` and
`Crystalline.tensorEnvelopeDPEquiv_structureMap`. -/
@[no_expose] public noncomputable def tensorEnvelopeDPEquiv (n : ℕ) :
    (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s (tensorPowerPresentation s f n)).object.carrier ≃+*
      setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialAlgebra
        (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).object (ι × Fin n) :=
  ((tensorEnvelopeDifferenceEquivData s f n).1.trans (addVariablesEquiv s f n)).trans
    (setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialReindexEquiv
      (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).object
      (Equiv.ulift (α := ι × Fin n)))

private theorem tensorEnvelopeDPEquiv_apply (n : ℕ)
    (y : (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s (tensorPowerPresentation s f n)).object.carrier) :
    tensorEnvelopeDPEquiv s f n y =
      setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialReindexEquiv
        (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).object (Equiv.ulift (α := ι × Fin n))
        (addVariablesEquiv s f n ((tensorEnvelopeDifferenceEquivData s f n).1 y)) :=
  rfl

/-- **The identification of the envelope of `J(n)` is a divided power morphism.** -/
public theorem tensorEnvelopeDPEquiv_isDPMorphism (n : ℕ) :
    DividedPowers.IsDPMorphism
      (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s
        (tensorPowerPresentation s f n)).object.dividedPowers
      (setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialDividedPowers
        (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).object (ι × Fin n))
      (tensorEnvelopeDPEquiv s f n).toRingHom :=
  DividedPowers.IsDPMorphism.comp
    (setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialDividedPowers
      (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).object (ι × Fin n))
    (setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialReindexEquiv_isDPMorphism
      (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).object (Equiv.ulift (α := ι × Fin n)))
    (DividedPowers.IsDPMorphism.comp
      (setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialDividedPowers
        (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).object (liftedDifferenceIndex (ι := ι) n))
      (addVariablesEquiv_spec s f n).1
      (tensorEnvelopeDifferenceEquivData s f n).property.2.1)

/-- **The inverse of the identification of the envelope of `J(n)` is a divided power morphism
too**, so the identification is an isomorphism of divided power rings and carries the divided
power differentials along in both directions. -/
public theorem tensorEnvelopeDPEquiv_symm_isDPMorphism (n : ℕ) :
    DividedPowers.IsDPMorphism
      (setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialDividedPowers
        (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).object (ι × Fin n))
      (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s
        (tensorPowerPresentation s f n)).object.dividedPowers
      (tensorEnvelopeDPEquiv s f n).symm.toRingHom :=
  DividedPowers.IsDPMorphism.comp
    (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s
      (tensorPowerPresentation s f n)).object.dividedPowers
    (DividedPowers.IsDPMorphism.comp
      (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s
        (tensorPowerPresentation s f n)).object.dividedPowers
      (tensorEnvelopeDifferenceEquivData s f n).property.2.2.1
      (addVariablesEquiv_spec s f n).2.1)
    (setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialReindexEquiv_symm_isDPMorphism
      (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).object (Equiv.ulift (α := ι × Fin n)))

/-- **The identification of the envelope of `J(n)` commutes with the two structure maps from
`A`**, so it is an isomorphism of divided power rings *over `A`* — which is what makes it a
morphism of divided power de Rham complexes relative to `A`. -/
public theorem tensorEnvelopeDPEquiv_structureMap (n : ℕ) (a : s.A) :
    tensorEnvelopeDPEquiv s f n
        ((polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s
          (tensorPowerPresentation s f n)).structureMap.toRingHom a) =
      algebraMap (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).object
        (setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialAlgebra
          (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).object (ι × Fin n))
        ((polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).structureMap.toRingHom a) := by
  have hstruct := congrArg (fun g : s.A →+* _ => g a)
    (tensorEnvelopeDifferenceEquivData s f n).property.2.2.2
  have hbase := congrArg (fun g : s.A →+* _ => g a)
    (differenceEnvelope s f n).algebraMap_comp
  have hbase₀ := congrArg (fun g : s.A →+* _ => g a)
    (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).algebraMap_comp
  rw [tensorEnvelopeDPEquiv_apply, show (tensorEnvelopeDifferenceEquivData s f n).1
        ((polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s
          (tensorPowerPresentation s f n)).structureMap.toRingHom a) =
      (differenceEnvelope s f n).algebraMap.toRingHom
        (MvPolynomial.C (algebraMap s.A (MvPolynomial ι s.A) a)) by
    simpa only [RingHom.comp_apply, RingEquiv.toRingHom_eq_coe,
      RingEquiv.coe_toRingHom] using hstruct.trans hbase.symm,
    (addVariablesEquiv_spec s f n).2.2.1,
    show (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).algebraMap.toRingHom
        (algebraMap s.A (MvPolynomial ι s.A) a) =
      (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).structureMap.toRingHom a from
      by simpa only [RingHom.comp_apply] using hbase₀,
    setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialReindexEquiv_algebraMap]

/-- **The identification carries the image of `ξ_i(j)` in the envelope of `J(n)` to the divided
power variable `ξ_i(j)`**, which is the clause of [Stacks, Tag 07L2] pinning down what the
isomorphism does to the difference coordinates, read before completion. -/
public theorem tensorEnvelopeDPEquiv_coprojectionDifference (n : ℕ) (q : ι × Fin n) :
    tensorEnvelopeDPEquiv s f n
        ((polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s
          (tensorPowerPresentation s f n)).algebraMap.toRingHom
          (coprojectionDifference s n q)) =
      dividedPowerPolynomialVariable (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).object q := by
  rw [tensorEnvelopeDPEquiv_apply, tensorEnvelopeDifferenceEquivData_algebraMap,
    tensorDifferenceCoordinates_coprojectionDifference, (addVariablesEquiv_spec s f n).2.2.2,
    setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialReindexEquiv_variable]
  rfl

/-- **The identification carries the image of the first coprojection `P → P ⊗ ⋯ ⊗ P` to the
coefficients**, which is the clause of [Stacks, Tag 07L2] saying that the isomorphism is one
over the structure map of `D(n)` as an algebra over `D`, read before completion. -/
public theorem tensorEnvelopeDPEquiv_coprojection (n : ℕ) (x : MvPolynomial ι s.A) :
    tensorEnvelopeDPEquiv s f n
        ((polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s
          (tensorPowerPresentation s f n)).algebraMap.toRingHom
          (mvPolynomialCoprojection s.A (0 : Fin (n + 1)) x)) =
      algebraMap (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).object
        (setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialAlgebra
          (polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).object (ι × Fin n))
        ((polynomialDividedPowerEnvelope s f).algebraMap.toRingHom x) := by
  rw [tensorEnvelopeDPEquiv_apply, tensorEnvelopeDifferenceEquivData_algebraMap,
    tensorDifferenceCoordinates_coprojection, (addVariablesEquiv_spec s f n).2.2.1,
    setIndexedDividedPowerPolynomialReindexEquiv_algebraMap]

end Crystalline

end

/-! ### The displayed equation

Equation 60.17.1.1 is the display `D(n) = lim_e D⟨ξ_i(j)⟩/p^e D⟨ξ_i(j)⟩` occurring in the
lemma above, and the theorem above is what proves it: the isomorphism it produces is the
displayed one, over the algebra structure `φ` of `D(n)` over `D` and carrying the image of
each `ξ_i(j)` to the divided power variable of the same name. The tag is therefore recorded
on that theorem rather than restated, which would duplicate the result under a second name.
-/

add_to_stacks 07L3 "equation 60.17.1.1, the display of this lemma: the isomorphism `e` \
produced here is `D(n) = lim_e D⟨ξ_i(j)⟩/p^e D⟨ξ_i(j)⟩`, over the algebra structure `φ` of \
`D(n)` over `D` and carrying the image of each `ξ_i(j)` to the divided power variable of the \
same name" Crystalline.exists_ringEquiv_pAdicCompletedDividedPowerPolynomial
